<header class="page-header">
  <div class="page-header-main">
    <div>
      <h1>Home</h1>
      <p>Wallpaper Engine Workshop</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="search-section" aria-label="Wallpaper search">
  <%- include('search-form') %>
</section>

<section class="home-intro">
  <div class="home-avatar"><i data-lucide="panels-top-left" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
  <div>
    <h2>Wallpaper Search</h2>
    <p>Search Wallpaper Engine Workshop items and open their download details.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="guide-section">
  <div class="guide-icon"><i data-lucide="check-circle-2" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
  <div>
    <h2>Before you begin</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Have a <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Steam account</a>
        with <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/431960/Wallpaper_Engine/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wallpaper Engine</a> in your library.
      </li>
      <li>Use a computer that can run Steam or SteamCMD.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="guide-section">
  <div class="guide-icon"><i data-lucide="terminal" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
  <div>
    <h2>Download workflow</h2>
    <h3>Using SteamCMD</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Install SteamCMD. Windows users can download
        <a href="https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/client/installer/steamcmd.zip" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">steamcmd.zip</a>.
        Linux and macOS users can follow the
        <a href="https://developer.valvesoftware.com/wiki/Zh/SteamCMD#Linux" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SteamCMD documentation</a>.
      </li>
      <li>Start SteamCMD and enter <code>login [yourusername]</code> without the brackets.</li>
      <li>Search here, open an item, then use the SteamCMD command shown on its detail page.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Using the Steam client on Windows</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Open Steam and sign in.</li>
      <li>Press <code>Win + R</code>, enter <code>steam://open/console</code>, and open it.</li>
      <li>Paste the command from the item detail page into the Steam console.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The Steam client method lets you monitor download progress directly.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="guide-section safety-callout">
  <div class="guide-icon"><i data-lucide="shield-alert" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
  <div>
    <h2>Open unfamiliar items carefully</h2>
    <p>Application and Web wallpapers can contain executable or remote content. This site is not responsible for losses caused by running Workshop items.</p>
  </div>
</section>

